[{"page":1,"text":"NOTICE OF A REGULAR\n\nPLANNING COMMISSION MEETING\n\nOctober 7, 2026, at 7:00 PM\n________________\nPUBLIC NOTICE is hereby given that the Vineyard Planning Commission will hold a regularly\nscheduled Planning Commission meeting on Wednesday, October 7, 2026, at 7:00 PM, in the\nCity Council Chambers at City Hall, 125 South Main Street, Vineyard, UT. This meeting can\nalso be viewed on our live stream page.\n\n1.\n\nCALL TO ORDER\n\n2.\n\nPRESENTATIONS, RECOGNITIONS, AWARDS, AND PROCLAMATIONS\n\n3.\n\nPUBLIC COMMENTS PC\nTime dedicated for public comment. Comments will be limited to three (3) minutes. No\nactions may be taken by the Planning Commission due to the need for proper public\nnoticing. Public comments can be submitted ahead of time to planning@vineyardutah.gov.\n\n4.\n\nBUSINESS ITEMS\n\n4.1. Conditional Use Permit - Coin Operated Claw and Arcade Machines\n\n4.2. Conditional Use Permit - Sunlight Bilingual Preschool\nThe applicant, Georgia Fenn, is requesting a conditional use permit approval for a\npreschool within the Fenn home, located at 38 W Sycamore Ln. The applicant’s\nhome is zoned R1-8, which allows a home preschool with 8-10 children as a\nconditional use.\n4.3. PLAN26-0012 Site Plan Application — Minor Amendment - Lot 6 / Vineyard Properties of\n\nUtah LLC Martin Snow\n\n4.4. PLAN26-0011 Site Plan Application - Minor Amendment Orchards Phase 7\n\n4.5. Senate Bill 284/City Code Compliance — Consideration of Ordinance No. 202611\n\n5.\n\nWORK SESSION\n\n6.\n\nSTAFF AND COMMISSION REPORTS\n\nPage 1 of 2; October 7, 2026, Planning Commission Agenda","ocr":false},{"page":2,"text":"7.\n\nADJOURNMENT\n\nThe next regularly scheduled meeting is on _November 4, 2026_\nThe public is invited to participate in all Planning Commission meetings. In compliance with the\nAmericans with Disabilities Act, individuals needing special accommodations during this public\nmeeting should notify the planning staff at least 24 hours prior to the meeting by calling (801)\n\n226-1929 or email at planning@vineyardutah.gov.\nThe foregoing notice and agenda were posted on the Utah Public Notice Website and Vineyard\nWebsite, posted at Vineyard City Hall, and delivered electronically to city staff and each member\nof the Planning Commission.\n\nOctober 1, 2026\n\nAGENDA NOTICING COMPLETED ON:\n\n/s/ Anthony Fletcher\n\nCERTIFIED (NOTICED) BY:\n\nAnthony Fletcher, Planner\n\nPage 2 of 2; October 7, 2026, Planning Commission Agenda","ocr":false}]